{"asks":[{"quote":"I did not add a preference for it. Every preference is a thing to test in both states, and the PRD says defaults should be right without a toggle. If you disagree, say so and I'll add it under Appearance.","question":"Should the activity strip have an Appearance preference, or remain always visible for one or more subagents?","kind":"decision","options":["Keep no preference","Add Appearance preference"]},{"quote":"Right now the strip shows the raw label. Do you want Strata to normalize these, for example always showing \"Explore: search for tests\" style labels, or should it show what the provider sent?","question":"Should Strata normalize subagent labels or display provider-supplied labels unchanged?","kind":"decision","options":["Normalize labels","Show provider labels"]},{"quote":"The alternative is moving finished activity into the Trace drawer so the conversation stays clean. I lean toward keeping it under the message, since that's where you'd look when reading the reply later, but this is the kind of thing you have stronger instincts on than I do. Tell me which you'd rather see and I'll do that one.","question":"Should finished activity remain under the message or move into the Trace drawer?","kind":"decision","options":["Keep under message","Move to Trace drawer"]},{"quote":"I capped it at eight visible rows with a \"and 12 more\" line, and the drawer shows all of them. Is eight the right number, or would you rather it show everything and scroll?","question":"Should the strip show eight rows with an overflow link or all rows with scrolling?","kind":"decision","options":["Eight plus overflow","Show all with scrolling"]},{"quote":"I'm treating a subagent that errors as finished, with a red dot, and not surfacing its error text in the strip. The error is in the trace. Is that enough, or do you want the error inline?","question":"Should subagent errors remain only in the trace or also appear inline in the activity strip?","kind":"decision","options":["Trace only","Show inline"]},{"quote":"The elapsed timer stops when T3 reports completion, not when the parent turn ends. That means a subagent that finished early keeps showing its own short time. I think that's correct.","question":"Should each subagent timer stop when that subagent completes, even if the parent turn continues?","kind":"question","options":[]},{"quote":"T3 does report it, so it's available. I left it out because the usage panel already totals it and per-row numbers made the strip busy. I can add it back if it's useful to you.","question":"Should each activity row display per-subagent token usage?","kind":"question","options":[]},{"quote":"Let me know if you'd rather I hold this until the link-opening change lands, since both touch the Conversation panel and there's a small merge risk in the message component.","question":"Should this work wait until the link-opening change lands or proceed now?","kind":"decision","options":["Proceed now","Wait for link change"]}]}
